WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.870
Yeast can turn sugar into
ethanol, slowly, in a warm vat.

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.830
A chemical plant can make exactly
the same molecule, quickly,

3
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.970
from steam and a gas that
comes from crude oil.

4
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.210
Same product, two completely
different routes.

5
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.770
So which way of making
ethanol is better?

6
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.310
In this mission, you'll
meet the alcohols,

7
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.740
and the group of atoms
that makes them alcohols.

8
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.510
You'll compare fermentation,
which uses yeast and sugar,

9
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.670
with the reaction
between ethene and steam.

10
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.150
Your mission: decide which
route to ethanol is better,

11
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.730
and explain why.
